# The folder above ignores every PNG and names its exceptions one at a time,
# because the default capture writes six frames nobody asked for and an
# untracked file there fails the gate's tree-clean step for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the push. The same rule applies here, and it lands on the
# same split docs/frames/effect-candidates/.gitignore lands on: which framing
# decides.
#
# THE WIDE FRAME IS COMMITTED AND THE CLOSE ONE IS NOT. Both are rendered and
# both were looked at -- issue #270 settled that a sheet and the built player
# disagree, so a candidate that is not read at 1600x900 has not been read. But
# only one of the two is an artefact worth keeping: the played/ frame is the one
# a decision is taken from, and the close/ frame is a supporting picture that
# regenerates in one command.
#
# THE WHOLE FOLDER IS TEMPORARY. It is the set of alternatives #284 signs from,
# and it goes when the signing does.
#
#   ./tools/capture-rung-candidates.ps1 -CloseOnly     redraws what is ignored
!played/*.png

# And the record the capture writes beside the frames it drew. The played/ one
# is kept, because check-docs.ps1 reads it where a commit date cannot answer;
# this directory is not committed at all, so its copy would be a record of
# pictures nobody has.
close/
